## Crew, worktrees and merge authority (firstmate)
A **firstmate** distro is installed and pinned at `__FM_ROOT__`. It owns what the gateway does not: a clean git worktree per task, a visible crew you can watch, fleet sync, and the merge authority that lands their work. Engage it when a job wants a crew rather than one worker — several tasks in parallel in their own checkouts, supervised to completion, landed as PRs or approved local merges — and for anything about worktree lifecycle or merging a fleet of branches back. Read `__FM_ROOT__/AGENTS.md` at that point, not before: it is large, and paying for it in a session that never spawns a crew is waste. Its `bin/` scripts are the deterministic half — `fm-fleet-view.sh` shows what is under way, `fm-spawn.sh` starts a crewmate, `fm-merge-local.sh` and `fm-pr-merge.sh` land work — and `fm-fleet-snapshot.sh --json` answers "what is running" without side effects. Tell the user you are engaging it, by name: **break-free -firstmate**. The two systems do not overlap: firstmate runs the crew, and the gateway still routes every model call, holds the tier floor, runs `verify` itself and gets the independent review. A firstmate crewmate is forbidden to delegate, so `delegate` and `run_plan` belong to you, the lead, never to a crewmate. `bf firstmate` starts a dedicated firstmate-led session when you want one; you do not need it to use the distro from here.
